{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/pulls/1591","id":5328247063,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUg-4R88AAAABPZaZFw","html_url":"https://github.com/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/pull/1591","diff_url":"https://github.com/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/pull/1591.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/pull/1591.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/issues/1591","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/pulls/1591/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/pulls/1591/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/issues/1591/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/cryptanalysis/statuses/4f724205866a334fb3ac137cb4aca2d57444a4f0","number":1591,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Implement native Curve25519 four-point recovery and version rejection criteria","user":{"login":"aburan28","id":1086874,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODY4NzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1086874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28","html_url":"https://github.com/aburan28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aburan28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The four-point torus compiler needs a public-input path from native basis output to checked curve decompositions. This adds bounded Rust rational-root and triangular-basis recovery, strict transcript framing, and arity 2–8 union-membership, rational-lift, sign and affine-sum checks. `prepare-tree` serializes the full-base input without invoking a solver; `recover-tree` consumes an existing transcript.\n\nActual-field M=1 native four-point controls match their complete singleton-base oracle: the member target yields one checked sum; the nonmember target yields none and the engine reports a unit basis. Each native process has four CPU seconds, five wall seconds and 768 MiB. These are functional controls, not full-base timings or independently certified absence results. [pcc:unverified]\n\nValidation: nine unit tests and one process-level immutable-input test pass, including actual-field roots, malformed/mixed protocol controls, and recovery of a known 454-variable assignment from a synthetic basis. That synthetic test does not establish solver discovery. Frozen transcripts, source archive, manifests and a rendered/inspected source-linked PDF are included. PCC-20261115-47a01f; earlier three-point controls are preserved under PCC-20261115-ec9f29. [pcc:unverified]\n\n`ROUTE_CRITERIA_V3.md` separates geometric, finite budgeted solver and asymptotic claims and gives an explicit corrected probability example. The original published criteria retain their exact bytes and PCC binding; the extension has a separate immutable snapshot, PCC-20261115-13362e. A timeout parks an implementation or informs its frozen probability test; it does not exclude all representations or index calculus. [pcc:unverified]\n\nShared-source dependency: https://github.com/isogeny-labs/crypto/pull/4364 at 98b6b736a53412ef86f02f9e789edc393af1fc20. TREE_DEPENDENCY.json pins both path dependencies and included source modules; the old three-leaf library hashes still match. Reproduction uses adjacent checkouts at that pin.\n\nThe full 454-variable/four-coset script is prepared but unsolved. Aggregate accounting, qualified isolated runtime, live capacity/spend readback, the proposed geometric proof and complete family/phase/rank bounds remain open. No exponent change, admitted timing comparison or cloud experiment is claimed. [pcc:unverified]\n\nFollows merged #1570. See the current study README, PROTOCOL.md, ROUTE_CRITERIA_V3.md and reports/recovery-v4/REPORT.md.\n\nArtifact publication is complete at consumer 0850536e87bfcfd09ed1feaa23208f0a4d925899. The trusted crypto artifact-autofix receipt at f8a7dbc5f7f2d82c3c2f9209d3dd7a1d025a9fb8 binds the original 121028 bytes and SHA-256 b17b53b7d259465ea7963670e6367474bbeec33cfd99ba6e8e066242cb2c8317. Maintained helpers register the same shared-store object as report.pdf; only the tracked copy was removed, with inspected local bytes retained. See reports/recovery-v4/PUBLISHING.md and STORE_RECEIPT.json.\n\nCurrent-head merge blockers are inherited: PCC-20261115-8d2645 passes raw text logs to a JSON recompute verifier, and the canonical ledger already exceeds the storage threshold on main. The latest store failure selects only pcc/ledger.jsonl; report.pdf is no longer an offender. Both issues are reported at issuecomment-6903927895. No policy exemption, claim rewrite or gate bypass is included. Required checks must pass before landing.\n\nInitial merged #1570 now has a partial publication-to-merge episode and matching lesson outcome under pr-checkin-20261116. Its final-head required checks completed after merge; missing original prompt/intervention timestamps remain explicit. [pcc:unverified]\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-15T23:12:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T01:35:32Z","closed_at":"2026-11-16T01:35:32Z","merged_at":"2026-11-16T01:35:32Z","merge_commit_sha":"2dee266203bedb19e302d2af64240815c679f085","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers"